Substituting $N = 33$, we have:
$|C_1| + |C_2| - |C_1 \cap C_2| \le 33$.
Rearranging to solve for $|C_1 \cap C_2|$:
$|C_1 \cap C_2| \ge |C_1| + |C_2| - 33$.

**Step 4: Minimize the intersection.**
To minimize $|C_1 \cap C_2|$, we need to minimize the sum $|C_1| + |C_2|$.
From Step 2, we established inequalities involving absolute values (cardinalities).
$|C_1| \ge 24$.
$|C_2| \ge 24$.
